  "slug": "clustering-dark-energy-064b",
  "summary": "Nonlinear spherical-collapse and N-body results probe model degeneracies that background and linear-level parametrizations leave unresolved.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is using nonlinear structure formation to discriminate beyond-ΛCDM models that background or linear descriptions cannot separate. Two papers argue that w(a) plus a linear sound speed does not fully specify clustering dark energy, and use spherical-collapse simulations, including a fully nonlinear fluid method that splits the dark energy action into kinetic and potential parts. ELEPHANT N-body simulations test whether halo merger-rate universality survives in f(R) chameleon and DGP gravity, with mass accretion deviating. A further paper generalizes scale-dependent equation-of-state dark matter to cosmological scales and finds it cannot be the sole dark matter component. The new element is nonlinear-regime discrimination of dark sector and gravity models.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
